1
00:00:07,041 --> 00:00:10,208
Ordinarily, this crystal should
change to a silver color.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:12,208
Huh? But doesn't that mean...

3
00:00:13,166 --> 00:00:15,083
Guess this thing's toast.

4
00:00:15,125 --> 00:00:18,083
Shouldn't we inform Alion of this?

5
00:00:18,083 --> 00:00:20,208
RUINS OF DISPOSAL
- Well, we can slap the usual
"nothing amiss" in today's report.

6
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:22,083
Well, we can slap the usual
"nothing amiss" in today's report.

7
00:00:22,083 --> 00:00:25,083
Nothing's out of place here either way.

8
00:00:25,166 --> 00:00:30,125
You don't think someone actually
made it out of these ruins alive, do you?

9
00:00:31,166 --> 00:00:33,208
That's not happening.

10
00:00:33,208 --> 00:00:38,166
After all, the Ruins of Disposal
have a survival rate of zero.

11
00:00:51,041 --> 00:00:53,208
Oh, you like the Lord of the Flies one?

12
00:00:53,208 --> 00:00:55,000
Lord of the Flies?

13
00:00:55,208 --> 00:00:58,125
He once turned an island
of monsters into his fortress

14
00:00:58,166 --> 00:01:00,208
and fended off all kinds of invasions,

15
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:06,000
making himself master of the demons
ostracized by the source of evil itself.

16
00:01:06,125 --> 00:01:09,208
The Lord of the Flies' army
was ultimately wiped out,

17
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:12,166
but since the way they went down
was just so cool,

18
00:01:12,166 --> 00:01:15,083
they're still popular to this day.

19
00:01:16,083 --> 00:01:17,166
Sir Tooka...

20
00:01:19,166 --> 00:01:24,041
Adding excess worries would
only interfere with his journey.

21
00:01:24,208 --> 00:01:27,000
So at least for a while...

22
00:01:27,125 --> 00:01:29,041
I should focus on being his sword.

23
00:01:32,041 --> 00:01:35,208
I'm not exactly a good hero right now.

24
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:43,041
A devil feels much more appropriate.

25
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:45,166
Goddess Vicius...

26
00:01:46,041 --> 00:01:48,208
You'll find yourself crushed
underfoot one day.

27
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:52,041
I'm going to be the one
to put you in your place.

28
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:56,041
Don't underestimate the dedication

29
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:58,208
of a man who's sold his soul.

30
00:03:29,083 --> 00:03:31,208
MAGNAR, WHITE CITADEL OF PROTECTION
- I can't believe the Five Dragoons
have been wiped out.

31
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:33,000
I can't believe the Five Dragoons
have been wiped out.

32
00:03:33,041 --> 00:03:35,166
INSIDE, WOLVES' RENDEZVOUS
- And you're certain it's true?

33
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:38,208
GANOZEA SIGMUS, MAGNAR'S WHITE WOLF KING
- I still find it hard to swallow that
Humanity's Strongest is no more.

34
00:03:38,208 --> 00:03:40,208
I still find it hard to swallow that
Humanity's Strongest is no more.

35
00:03:41,208 --> 00:03:44,166
JIN ROWAN, ULZA'S MONSTER SLAYER KING
- I identified the corpses
of the Five Dragoons personally.

36
00:03:44,208 --> 00:03:46,125
We are looking into the matter.

37
00:03:46,166 --> 00:03:50,041
Right. Any pertinent information from Alion?

38
00:03:50,083 --> 00:03:52,125
YUSEF WOLLETTA, ALION'S STEADFAST KING
- Goddess?

39
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:53,208
GODDESS VICIUS, ALION KINGDOM

40
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:55,041
GODDESS VICIUS, ALION KINGDOM
- Apparently the Black Dragon Knights
were pursuing Seras Ashrain.

41
00:03:55,083 --> 00:03:58,083
Apparently the Black Dragon Knights
were pursuing Seras Ashrain.

42
00:03:58,125 --> 00:04:01,000
ALMA SENTNOKIA
YONATO'S QUEEN, KEEPER OF THE SACRED EYES
- Neah's former knight captain?

43
00:04:01,041 --> 00:04:03,166
Do we have any clue where
she went afterward?

44
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:07,041
At the scene, we found what we believe to be

45
00:04:07,083 --> 00:04:10,083
the bloody, torn remnants of her clothes.

46
00:04:10,083 --> 00:04:11,166
Judging by the amount of blood,

47
00:04:11,166 --> 00:04:14,083
we believe she was grievously wounded.

48
00:04:14,083 --> 00:04:19,000
You're suggesting there's a chance they
killed each other and she's already dead.

49
00:04:19,041 --> 00:04:21,041
Anyway, speaking of Neah,

50
00:04:21,083 --> 00:04:24,125
I heard Holy Emperor Ortola
passed away last night.

51
00:04:24,125 --> 00:04:28,041
I also heard he lost his mind
just before his death.

52
00:04:28,208 --> 00:04:32,208
I couldn't care less about the coward who
sold out his own country without a fight.

53
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:34,125
Either way,

54
00:04:34,125 --> 00:04:39,125
the Black Dragon Knights were our best
hope against the Great Demon Empire.

55
00:04:39,166 --> 00:04:43,208
Losing them is a major
blow to our Holy Alliance.

56
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:45,000
It so follows

57
00:04:45,041 --> 00:04:49,125
that the heroes from another world
will play an even more important role now.

58
00:04:49,166 --> 00:04:52,208
FALKENDOTZINE MIRADIASORDZIT
MIRA'S BEAUTIFUL MAD EMPEROR
- When great evil comes, Alion flourishes.

59
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:56,166
Oh my. I do believe it sounds
like you're implying something.

60
00:04:57,041 --> 00:04:59,083
Whenever the source of evil itself appears,

61
00:04:59,125 --> 00:05:02,041
all nations are forced to rely upon Alion.

62
00:05:02,041 --> 00:05:04,083
There's nothing we can do about that.

63
00:05:04,083 --> 00:05:07,041
Every living soul in this world is hampered

64
00:05:07,041 --> 00:05:11,166
by the demon king essence, leaving them
unable to harness their full power.

65
00:05:13,166 --> 00:05:15,125
What about the legend of the God Slayer?

66
00:05:16,166 --> 00:05:21,166
Pardon, but what could possibly lead
you to bring up such a story now?

67
00:05:21,208 --> 00:05:23,000
Are you well?

68
00:05:24,125 --> 00:05:27,041
Sorry for interrupting the conversation.

69
00:05:27,083 --> 00:05:28,125
Do continue.

70
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:31,166
I'd like to ask you all once more.

71
00:05:31,208 --> 00:05:36,125
Do you believe the demise of the Five
Dragoons was the work of Seras Ashrain?

72
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:41,041
Excuse me.

73
00:05:43,166 --> 00:05:47,041
Apparently someone in Ulza
is claiming they were responsible

74
00:05:47,041 --> 00:05:49,000
for eliminating the Black Dragon Knights.

75
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:55,125
They call themselves
the cursed magic users of Ashint.

76
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:57,208
MONROY'S BLOODSPORT CHAMPION

77
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:00,208
MONROY'S BLOODSPORT CHAMPION
- The Land of Golden-Eyed Monsters
lies further north from here.

78
00:06:00,208 --> 00:06:01,208
The Land of Golden-Eyed Monsters
lies further north from here.

79
00:06:03,041 --> 00:06:05,041
No signs of pursuers, huh?

80
00:06:06,166 --> 00:06:09,125
I expect this city will be our
best option to make preparations.

81
00:06:11,125 --> 00:06:12,125
What's that?

82
00:06:12,166 --> 00:06:15,000
The bloodsport colosseum.

83
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:16,083
Bloodsport colosseum?

84
00:06:16,083 --> 00:06:17,083
Yes.

85
00:06:17,208 --> 00:06:21,041
It's an arena where slaves
and mercenaries kill each other.

86
00:06:21,166 --> 00:06:24,000
The fighters are called bloodsport warriors,

87
00:06:24,041 --> 00:06:26,083
and they can earn rewards by winning matches.

88
00:06:26,166 --> 00:06:29,125
So like the gladiators of ancient Rome.

89
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:33,083
The duke and the mercenary's
guild run the place.

90
00:06:34,125 --> 00:06:37,041
It's now a prime source
of entertainment for the masses,

91
00:06:37,083 --> 00:06:41,166
but it started as a place for the
mercenary's guild to assess fighters.

92
00:06:44,083 --> 00:06:46,041
This looks like a good inn.

93
00:06:46,208 --> 00:06:48,166
So as not to waste travel funds,

94
00:06:48,208 --> 00:06:51,083
I feel we should get but one room...

95
00:06:51,125 --> 00:06:54,125
unless you're against it, my liege.

96
00:06:55,041 --> 00:06:57,000
You know I'm a man, right?

97
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:02,166
That's not a problem.

98
00:07:03,041 --> 00:07:05,000
Then I'll guess we'll go with one room.

99
00:07:05,083 --> 00:07:06,208
O-Okay.

100
00:07:10,083 --> 00:07:11,166
As expected of the capital,

101
00:07:11,166 --> 00:07:12,208
this place is pretty packed.

102
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:14,083
Hey, did you hear about
the Black Dragon Knights?

103
00:07:14,125 --> 00:07:15,166
- Hey, did you hear about
the Black Dragon Knights?
- From here, I can...

104
00:07:15,166 --> 00:07:17,208
Got any new info on that?

105
00:07:17,208 --> 00:07:21,125
You know how they say Seras Ashrain
killed the Five Dragoons?

106
00:07:21,166 --> 00:07:23,125
Well, apparently she's dead!

107
00:07:24,125 --> 00:07:26,041
Did they take each other out?

108
00:07:26,083 --> 00:07:27,125
- Are you alright?
- Nah, she just lost and fell in battle.

109
00:07:27,125 --> 00:07:30,000
Nah, she just lost and fell in battle.

110
00:07:30,041 --> 00:07:32,125
- Thank you.
- Then who killed them?

111
00:07:32,125 --> 00:07:36,041
They're saying Ashint got the Five Dragoons.

112
00:07:36,041 --> 00:07:37,041
Ashint?

113
00:07:37,041 --> 00:07:41,041
Oh, the cursed magic users everyone's
been talking about lately?

114
00:07:41,166 --> 00:07:46,083
Word is they're going around claiming they
killed the Dragoons with their curses.

115
00:07:46,083 --> 00:07:47,083
- Word is they're going around claiming they
killed the Dragoons with their curses.
- What do you think?

116
00:07:47,208 --> 00:07:50,125
I've heard rumors about them as of late.

117
00:07:50,125 --> 00:07:54,083
Apparently they worship the god of curses.

118
00:07:56,083 --> 00:07:59,000
We are the guardians of Ashint!

119
00:07:59,041 --> 00:08:01,125
ASHINT SOLDIERS
- The soldiers who protect Sir Muaji,
progeny of the curse god!

120
00:08:01,166 --> 00:08:03,083
The soldiers who protect Sir Muaji,
progeny of the curse god!

121
00:08:03,125 --> 00:08:04,208
We are his Curse Soldiers.

122
00:08:05,125 --> 00:08:07,166
Now, clear a seat for us.

123
00:08:09,125 --> 00:08:11,083
Hurry up and bring us some booze!

124
00:08:11,125 --> 00:08:14,083
We are the saviors of Ulza!

125
00:08:14,083 --> 00:08:16,041
They hardly seem like a threat.

126
00:08:16,041 --> 00:08:19,000
But I guess it works out for me if
they're taking responsibility

127
00:08:19,041 --> 00:08:20,125
for offing the Black Dragon Knights.

128
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:24,041
Must've really cursed them to death, huh?

129
00:08:24,041 --> 00:08:26,208
Well, even if someone else did the deed,

130
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:29,208
these guys could always just say
it was the work of their curses.

131
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:31,208
I see. That's one way to look at it.

132
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:35,000
Man, speaking of people
who could take on the Dragoons...

133
00:08:35,041 --> 00:08:37,125
The Dragon Slayer and the
leopardman at the colosseum.

134
00:08:37,166 --> 00:08:39,000
What about the Witch of Taboos?

135
00:08:39,041 --> 00:08:40,083
What, the witch?

136
00:08:40,083 --> 00:08:43,125
Yeah! She's a dark elf, right?

137
00:08:43,125 --> 00:08:47,041
Though no one's seen her
in over a decade now.

138
00:08:47,041 --> 00:08:51,041
Actually, someone right here
in the royal capital has met her.

139
00:08:51,041 --> 00:08:54,083
Mind telling me more about that?

140
00:08:54,083 --> 00:08:56,041
Who the hell are you, man?

141
00:08:56,041 --> 00:08:59,041
Oh, first, each of you can
order two drinks of your choice.

142
00:08:59,041 --> 00:09:01,208
Place an order for something to eat, too.

143
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:03,083
My treat, of course.

144
00:09:03,125 --> 00:09:04,208
All right, young man, have a seat!

145
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:07,083
Hey, lady! Bring us another round!

146
00:09:08,166 --> 00:09:11,166
So, the person who claims
they've met the Witch of Taboos

147
00:09:11,208 --> 00:09:14,208
is apparently Monroy's
strongest bloodsport warrior.

148
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:17,083
How would I go about meeting this person?

149
00:09:17,083 --> 00:09:21,083
That monster's gotta be at
the bloodsport colosseum, right?

150
00:09:21,208 --> 00:09:26,083
If you talk to Duke Zuan,
the guy who runs the place—

151
00:09:27,041 --> 00:09:29,125
Boy, you're in luck.

152
00:09:32,166 --> 00:09:35,083
That right there is Monroy's
strongest bloodsport warrior...

153
00:09:37,083 --> 00:09:38,208
EVE SPEED
LEOPARDMAN BLOODSPORT WARRIOR
- Eve Speed.

154
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:40,125
EVE SPEED
LEOPARDMAN BLOODSPORT WARRIOR

155
00:09:43,083 --> 00:09:45,208
Can I treat you to anything?

156
00:09:47,041 --> 00:09:48,166
I heard the rumors about you

157
00:09:48,208 --> 00:09:51,041
and was hoping to meet you.

158
00:09:51,041 --> 00:09:54,083
My name is Hati. I'm a mercenary.

159
00:09:54,166 --> 00:09:56,083
Eve Speed.

160
00:09:57,083 --> 00:09:59,041
You can really put it away, huh?

161
00:09:59,083 --> 00:10:01,000
Oh, right, you're a bloodsport warrior.

162
00:10:01,041 --> 00:10:02,083
State your business.

163
00:10:04,041 --> 00:10:08,000
You didn't come over here
because I'm a bloodsport warrior.

164
00:10:08,041 --> 00:10:09,000
Or am I wrong?

165
00:10:09,041 --> 00:10:10,166
Saw right through me, huh?

166
00:10:10,166 --> 00:10:12,083
Then I'll be upfront.

167
00:10:12,166 --> 00:10:15,125
Do you know where the Witch of Taboos is?

168
00:10:16,083 --> 00:10:19,125
So you're the type to believe
rumors flying around, huh?

169
00:10:19,208 --> 00:10:24,125
It's true I ventured to the Land of
Golden-Eyed Monsters where she dwells,

170
00:10:24,208 --> 00:10:27,125
but I've never met the witch.

171
00:10:27,125 --> 00:10:32,041
So you're saying that you don't
know where the Witch of Taboos is?

172
00:10:32,041 --> 00:10:34,000
Sorry, but I don't.

173
00:10:34,125 --> 00:10:35,166
I see.

174
00:10:36,166 --> 00:10:38,208
Why do you seek the Witch of Taboos?

175
00:10:39,083 --> 00:10:41,083
Curiosity, I suppose?

176
00:10:41,083 --> 00:10:43,125
I dream of being a scholar in the future.

177
00:10:43,166 --> 00:10:47,000
So I'd love to hire a mercenary
and pay the witch a visit.

178
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:50,041
That's not a place you waltz into
and come back alive.

179
00:10:50,166 --> 00:10:52,125
I know this sounds rude,

180
00:10:52,166 --> 00:10:55,000
but I doubt you'd last three days there.

181
00:10:55,166 --> 00:10:58,166
I appreciate your concern.

182
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:01,125
Hmph. I'm just doing you a favor.

183
00:11:02,125 --> 00:11:04,166
From what I can tell, you're still young.

184
00:11:04,166 --> 00:11:07,000
You should cherish your life.

185
00:11:07,083 --> 00:11:12,083
Though maybe that rings hollow
coming from a bloodsport warrior.

186
00:11:17,166 --> 00:11:19,208
She was lying.

187
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:23,125
So by denying it,
she actually outed herself to us.

188
00:11:23,166 --> 00:11:25,000
Yes. This has to mean...

189
00:11:25,041 --> 00:11:29,000
Eve Speed knows the whereabouts
of the Witch of Taboos.

190
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:30,125
Oh no.

191
00:11:30,166 --> 00:11:32,041
What's the matter?

192
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:36,000
I forgot to bring Piggymaru food.

193
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:37,000
Huh?

194
00:11:37,083 --> 00:11:39,208
It's been a while, but I guess I'll use that.

195
00:11:52,208 --> 00:11:55,000
Slightly hardened bread...

196
00:11:55,041 --> 00:11:56,208
and is this cheese?

197
00:11:59,166 --> 00:12:01,083
It's delicious.

198
00:12:02,041 --> 00:12:03,166
What is this?

199
00:12:03,166 --> 00:12:06,208
Is it a common food in your world?

200
00:12:08,125 --> 00:12:09,125
It is.

201
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:12,083
P-Pardon me.

202
00:12:12,083 --> 00:12:14,166
Enjoying this otherworldy snack?

203
00:12:14,208 --> 00:12:18,000
Yes. It's so good it made me smile.

204
00:12:18,041 --> 00:12:19,166
I'd love to give you more,

205
00:12:19,208 --> 00:12:22,125
but sadly I can't will it
to produce the same thing.

206
00:12:23,125 --> 00:12:25,041
A transparent bag...

207
00:12:25,041 --> 00:12:27,166
Are these letters scribed on it?

208
00:12:28,083 --> 00:12:30,083
It's pretty.

209
00:12:42,166 --> 00:12:46,000
Maybe it seems more alluring
because it's not from your world.

210
00:12:48,166 --> 00:12:51,083
Now, let's consider our plan moving forward.

211
00:12:51,083 --> 00:12:52,041
Yes.

212
00:12:52,083 --> 00:12:54,208
First up, the Witch of Taboos' location.

213
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:58,166
I hope we can find a way to get that
bloodsport warrior to tell us, but...

214
00:12:58,166 --> 00:13:02,000
Shall we try gathering information
on her tomorrow?

215
00:13:03,083 --> 00:13:06,208
What would a bloodsport warrior
value most after their life?

216
00:13:06,208 --> 00:13:08,125
Typically money?

217
00:13:08,125 --> 00:13:12,125
They can buy their freedom
if they have the funds.

218
00:13:12,208 --> 00:13:16,000
Though it seems to require a vast sum.

219
00:13:16,083 --> 00:13:19,000
A vast sum, huh?

220
00:13:23,208 --> 00:13:25,041
Anything new?

221
00:13:25,166 --> 00:13:26,166
No.

222
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:30,041
Hang in there a little longer.

223
00:13:30,041 --> 00:13:33,000
I promise I'll get you out of here.

224
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:41,125
Silfigzea, Ferillbanger, Willozega.

225
00:13:47,083 --> 00:13:51,041
Every time I see this, it reminds me of
a magical girl's transformation scene.

226
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:07,083
What gorgeous swordsmanship.

227
00:14:10,125 --> 00:14:14,041
No wonder Civit had high
hopes for fighting her.

228
00:14:21,125 --> 00:14:26,125
So, is there any kind of trick
to close combat?

229
00:14:26,125 --> 00:14:28,041
Are you interested?

230
00:14:28,083 --> 00:14:30,166
I rely too much on my skill as things stand.

231
00:14:30,166 --> 00:14:33,125
I might need it at some point.

232
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:35,083
I understand.

233
00:14:35,208 --> 00:14:39,166
We'll start with using minimal
motion to lock down your opponent.

234
00:14:42,041 --> 00:14:43,041
What is it?

235
00:14:43,083 --> 00:14:48,041
Well, back when I was captain of the knights,
I often trained the members like this.

236
00:14:48,125 --> 00:14:51,083
So I suddenly felt nostalgic.

237
00:14:54,125 --> 00:14:55,125
Now then...

238
00:14:57,041 --> 00:14:59,000
Please assault me.

239
00:15:03,208 --> 00:15:05,166
Oh, no, um...

240
00:15:05,208 --> 00:15:11,166
I only meant in terms of
using force to defeat me.

241
00:15:12,041 --> 00:15:14,125
I know. Here I come.

242
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:21,208
Now, if you do this as well...

243
00:15:21,208 --> 00:15:24,000
You don't need any weapons for this,

244
00:15:24,041 --> 00:15:26,208
and you can use it on opponents
you don't want to harm seriously.

245
00:15:26,208 --> 00:15:29,083
You can hone this move
in a few short days...

246
00:15:29,166 --> 00:15:31,125
I-I'm sorry!

247
00:15:31,166 --> 00:15:34,083
I got too close and I'm all sweaty!

248
00:15:34,125 --> 00:15:35,125
Don't worry about it.

249
00:15:35,166 --> 00:15:37,125
If you don't want to get so close,

250
00:15:37,166 --> 00:15:39,166
then please at least teach me the form.

251
00:15:40,041 --> 00:15:44,208
S-Sir Tooka, are you all right
with me teaching you like this?

252
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:46,208
Yeah, I'm fine with it.

253
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:48,041
Let's keep going.

254
00:15:52,041 --> 00:15:53,125
Sir Tooka's...

255
00:15:58,166 --> 00:16:00,166
What a strange sensation.

256
00:16:00,166 --> 00:16:03,208
It feels like part of him
is blending into me...

257
00:16:07,125 --> 00:16:09,041
What am I...?

258
00:16:11,125 --> 00:16:13,166
It doesn't look like anyone is watching.

259
00:16:14,083 --> 00:16:18,083
Even if I do have affection for him,
how could I do such a dirty, lewd thing?

260
00:16:18,125 --> 00:16:19,125
Do you have a moment?

261
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:26,208
Since when—?!

262
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:29,041
H-How long has Sir Tooka been here?

263
00:16:29,208 --> 00:16:32,125
I'm sorry I didn't notice you were there.

264
00:16:32,166 --> 00:16:35,000
Did you need me for something?

265
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:37,166
Yeah, I noticed my clothes were missing,

266
00:16:37,166 --> 00:16:38,208
so I wanted to check with you.

267
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:40,083
My apologies!

268
00:16:40,125 --> 00:16:44,083
I know I didn't ask, but I thought I
would wash them with mine!

269
00:16:44,083 --> 00:16:46,083
You don't mind if I ask you to do that?

270
00:16:46,125 --> 00:16:47,208
I don't mind at all!

271
00:16:47,208 --> 00:16:49,208
I'm used to washing clothes.

272
00:17:03,166 --> 00:17:08,041
That's what a truly kind person looks like.

273
00:17:12,208 --> 00:17:16,000
Seras is diligently trying
to become my sword.

274
00:17:16,041 --> 00:17:19,166
She's suppressing all kinds of emotions
to perform her role for me.

275
00:17:22,125 --> 00:17:24,041
I should be grateful.

276
00:17:26,041 --> 00:17:27,041
Sir Tooka?

277
00:17:28,208 --> 00:17:30,208
Are you still awake?

278
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:32,208
I just couldn't sleep.

279
00:17:32,208 --> 00:17:34,083
That's not good.

280
00:17:34,125 --> 00:17:35,125
In that case...

281
00:17:39,083 --> 00:17:41,041
These are a type of medicinal herb.

282
00:17:41,125 --> 00:17:43,000
Do they help you go to sleep?

283
00:17:43,166 --> 00:17:45,041
That's correct.

284
00:17:45,041 --> 00:17:47,041
Looks like there are several varieties.

285
00:17:47,041 --> 00:17:51,125
Yes. These herbs have a similar color,
but they have the opposite effect.

286
00:17:51,166 --> 00:17:56,083
Drinking these is said to grant
you vigor and leave you excited.

287
00:17:57,041 --> 00:17:58,125
I'm sorry.

288
00:17:58,125 --> 00:18:00,125
Um, I didn't mean anything by that.

289
00:18:00,166 --> 00:18:02,000
I know.

290
00:18:02,125 --> 00:18:03,166
Medicinal herbs, huh?

291
00:18:05,208 --> 00:18:07,000
Wait a minute.

292
00:18:15,041 --> 00:18:17,041
Oh, that smells good.

293
00:18:17,125 --> 00:18:20,083
Would you like a taste
before we add the herbs?

294
00:18:20,083 --> 00:18:21,083
Yes, please!

295
00:18:23,125 --> 00:18:24,166
It's delicious!

296
00:18:25,083 --> 00:18:28,083
So just putting this
in hot water creates soup?

297
00:18:28,125 --> 00:18:30,208
Seems like an excellent portable meal.

298
00:18:31,125 --> 00:18:33,125
Let's try adding the herbs next.

299
00:18:33,125 --> 00:18:35,041
Yes, right away.

300
00:18:40,166 --> 00:18:42,000
It's done.

301
00:18:42,083 --> 00:18:45,083
Shall I drink the one we
used the wrong amount in?

302
00:18:45,083 --> 00:18:47,125
No, I'll drink it!

303
00:18:47,166 --> 00:18:50,000
Please let me take responsibility.

304
00:18:50,041 --> 00:18:51,000
Okay...

305
00:18:54,083 --> 00:18:57,041
It may be a bit thick after
using the wrong amount,

306
00:18:57,041 --> 00:18:59,083
but drinking this is refreshing.

307
00:18:59,166 --> 00:19:01,000
Refreshing?

308
00:19:01,041 --> 00:19:02,125
Isn't it?

309
00:19:02,166 --> 00:19:05,083
This herb typically...

310
00:19:07,041 --> 00:19:08,208
Did you use the wrong one?

311
00:19:08,208 --> 00:19:10,000
Yes...

312
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:15,041
Sir Tooka, I'm truly sorry.

313
00:19:15,041 --> 00:19:16,000
It's fine.

314
00:19:16,041 --> 00:19:20,000
Thanks to that, I can read through
a bit more of this tonight.

315
00:19:21,125 --> 00:19:25,000
Damn, I can't seem to settle down.

316
00:19:25,083 --> 00:19:26,125
Um...

317
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:30,000
Is there anything I can do for you?

318
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:38,000
Just get some sleep.

319
00:19:38,083 --> 00:19:41,166
We have intel to gather tomorrow.

320
00:19:44,083 --> 00:19:45,125
Sir Tooka.

321
00:19:46,166 --> 00:19:48,166
May I ask you something?

322
00:19:49,041 --> 00:19:50,083
What is it?

323
00:19:50,083 --> 00:19:52,208
Are you resistant to temptation?

324
00:19:53,083 --> 00:19:55,083
Oh, I mean, um...

325
00:19:55,125 --> 00:20:00,125
Well, I might be resistant for now.

326
00:20:02,041 --> 00:20:04,041
For now?

327
00:20:04,208 --> 00:20:08,083
Right now, my revenge takes
priority over all else.

328
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:13,041
I think that makes it difficult for me
to turn my attention elsewhere.

329
00:20:14,083 --> 00:20:16,041
In a sense, it's binding me.

330
00:20:16,125 --> 00:20:17,125
Binding you?

331
00:20:18,041 --> 00:20:22,208
Though once I achieve my revenge,
I should be able to focus on other things.

332
00:20:23,083 --> 00:20:24,166
Until then...

333
00:20:25,208 --> 00:20:28,166
Well, I guess it's like I'm cursed.

334
00:20:35,166 --> 00:20:41,208
I'll do everything in my power to help
release you from that curse as soon as we can.

335
00:20:43,083 --> 00:20:45,208
Yeah, I'll be counting on you.

336
00:20:46,125 --> 00:20:49,000
Yes, my liege.

337
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:55,125
BLOODSPORT COLOSSEUM

338
00:20:56,208 --> 00:20:58,125
I've returned.

339
00:20:59,041 --> 00:21:00,083
How did it go?

340
00:21:00,083 --> 00:21:02,208
As you'd expect concerning
a popular bloodsport warrior,

341
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:06,208
everyone was happy to talk
when I brought up Eve Speed.

342
00:21:07,166 --> 00:21:09,166
She used to be a slave,

343
00:21:09,208 --> 00:21:12,125
and her slaver sold her to the colosseum.

344
00:21:12,208 --> 00:21:15,125
Since leopardmen are uncommon,

345
00:21:15,166 --> 00:21:17,166
she was a hit from her first fight.

346
00:21:17,208 --> 00:21:21,208
Also, she hasn't lost a single
match in the three years since.

347
00:21:22,208 --> 00:21:27,083
Did you already hear that
tomorrow's her final fight?

348
00:21:27,083 --> 00:21:28,041
Yes.

349
00:21:28,083 --> 00:21:31,125
Which means she's already earned
enough to buy her own freedom.

350
00:21:32,041 --> 00:21:35,125
That'll make using money
to negotiate rather difficult.

351
00:21:36,083 --> 00:21:38,166
Moreover, I learned something concerning.

352
00:21:39,125 --> 00:21:45,125
Apparently, she'd already earned the funds
to buy her own freedom two years ago.

353
00:21:46,083 --> 00:21:47,166
Then why...?

354
00:21:49,166 --> 00:21:52,125
She's trying to buy someone else's.

355
00:21:53,041 --> 00:21:54,041
A child?

356
00:21:55,208 --> 00:21:58,000
She wants her freedom too.

357
00:21:58,125 --> 00:22:02,041
There's one more thing you should know.

358
00:22:02,125 --> 00:22:05,166
The majority of previous bloodsport champions

359
00:22:05,166 --> 00:22:07,166
have died during their final matches.

360
00:22:08,000 --> 00:22:10,041
I heard about that too.

361
00:22:10,083 --> 00:22:12,083
But isn't that just the result

362
00:22:12,125 --> 00:22:15,208
of getting pitted against
a challenging opponent for a finale?

363
00:22:16,208 --> 00:22:19,083
It seems there's more to it than that.

364
00:22:21,125 --> 00:22:24,125
I heard the duke running
the bloodsport colosseum

365
00:22:24,166 --> 00:22:28,125
arranges for the champions
to be at a disadvantage.

366
00:22:37,083 --> 00:22:39,208
Then that might be our lead.

367
00:24:10,166 --> 00:24:14,208
TOGETHER WITH THE LORD OF FLIES

